# Rebuild and relaunch after every task

When you finish any task that changes code or resources in this repo, do these steps before you report back. Do them in order.

1. **Close every running instance.** Stop every process whose executable path or command line contains `\GitHub\Shideh\`. That includes `SauronHarness.exe`, `copilot-runtime.exe`, and their child processes.
   ```powershell
   Get-CimInstance Win32_Process | Where-Object { $_.ExecutablePath -like '*\GitHub\Shideh\*' -or $_.CommandLine -like '*\GitHub\Shideh\*' } | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_.ProcessId -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
   ```
2. **Clean rebuild.** Delete `out`, then run `npm run build-fast` from the repo root. Use `build-fast` instead of `npm run compile`, because `compile`'s type check currently fails on unrelated stale tests.
   ```powershell
   Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .\out -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
   npm run build-fast
   ```
   If the build fails, fix the error, or report it if it isn't caused by your change. Do not launch a stale build.
3. **Relaunch.** Start `scripts\code.bat` in the background so it doesn't block the session.
   ```powershell
   Start-Process cmd.exe -ArgumentList '/c','scripts\code.bat' -WorkingDirectory (Get-Location) -WindowStyle Hidden
   ```
4. **Verify.** Wait about 20 seconds, then confirm `SauronHarness` processes are running from `\GitHub\Shideh\`. Mention the result in your final reply.

Skip these steps only for tasks that don't touch the app, such as answering questions or editing docs.
